; Regression test against a real, GCC-compiled RISC-V ELF (not a
; hand-assembled synthetic one). See examples/main.c for the source and
; examples/README.md for the exact compiler invocation used to produce
; Inputs/real_main_rv64.elf. The binary keeps its symbol table (built
; without -s), so this also exercises objdump-style symbol annotation on
; branch and jal targets.
RUN: %decoder %S/Inputs/real_main_rv64.elf | FileCheck %s

CHECK: Disassembly of section .text:
CHECK: bne   a5, a3, 1014c <main+0x8>
CHECK: c.bnez  a4, 10164 <main+0x20>
CHECK: jal   ra, 10144 <main>
CHECK: c.j   10188 <_start+0x8>
